
class Solution {
    static List<Integer> firstNegInt(int arr[], int k) {
        int n = arr.length;
        List<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();
        Deque<Integer> dq = new LinkedList<>();
        int i=0,j=0;
        while(j<n){
            if(arr[j]<0){
                dq.addLast(arr[j]);
            }
            
            if(j-i+1 == k){
                if(!dq.isEmpty()){
                    list.add(dq.peekFirst());
                }
                else{
                    list.add(0);
                }
            
            if(arr[i]<0 && !dq.isEmpty()){
                dq.pollFirst();
            }
            i++;
            }
            j++;
        }
        return list;
    }
}




🪟 First Negative Integer in Every Window (Sliding Window)
🔹 Problem Summary

Given an array arr[] and window size k, find the first negative number in every contiguous subarray of size k.
If a window has no negative number, return 0.

🔹 Approach Used

Sliding Window + Deque

🔹 Why Deque?

Deque allows O(1) insertion and deletion from both ends

Needed to:

Store negative elements

Remove elements when they go out of the window

🔹 Algorithm (Step-by-Step)

Use two pointers:

i → start of window

j → end of window

Traverse array using j

If arr[j] < 0

Add it to deque using addLast()

When window size becomes k (j - i + 1 == k):

If deque is not empty → add peekFirst() to answer list

Else → add 0

Before sliding window:

If arr[i] is negative and equals deque front

Remove it using pollFirst()

Move window forward:

i++, j++
